# Auto-detected by trivy with no flag needed (default --ignorefile is
# .trivyignore) -- deliberately global rather than path-scoped, because
# trivy-action's own path-scoped `.trivyignore.yaml` + trivyignores input
# does not correctly re-apply the severity threshold before deciding the
# job's exit code when format is sarif (observed: findings well below
# CRITICAL/HIGH still failed the job). Only two IDs, each with a narrow,
# documented reason -- see deploy/kustomize/base/rbac.yaml and
# backend/Dockerfile.dev / frontend/Dockerfile.dev for the rationale in
# context.

# resources: ["*"] on kubemg-custom-resource-{view,edit} only ever reaches
# the enumerated, non-core API groups those ClusterRoles list (Gateway API +
# Istio) -- never the core group, where Secrets live.
AVD-KSV-0046

# backend/Dockerfile.dev and frontend/Dockerfile.dev are dev-only images
# built solely by `make up` / docker-compose.yml against a bind-mounted
# source tree and a shared dependency-cache volume; running as the image's
# default root keeps those volumes writable without matching host UIDs.
# Neither Dockerfile is built or shipped anywhere else.
AVD-DS-0002
